{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Edgeu8wfKicV4RF8pbP6iL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed \"best\" tier predictions for each planned experiment in the experiment plan. Let me go through each planned experiment and provide predictions consistent with the \"best\" tier definition.\n\nLet me identify all planned experiments:\n1. exp-001: Multi-judge formality pairwise (planned)\n2. exp-002: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (planned)\n3. exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges (planned)\n4. exp-005: Pairwise RATE control (planned)\n5. exp-006: Scaled replication n=300-500 (planned)\n\n\n6. exp-007b: Verbosity — partially complete but blocked on API scoring\n7. exp-008: Register — needs n=100 generation and API scoring\n8. exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control (planned)\n9. exp-013: Human NLI validation (planned)\n\nI'm noticing a discrepancy with exp-013 — it shows as planned in the experiment plan but appears completed in the registry with a kappa value of 0.4304. Let me check if this is a status mismatch or if the registry is more current.\n\nLooking at the registry entry, exp-013 is marked DONE with the kappa score and conclusion about it serving as a conservative lower-bound estimate for false positive rates. So it's actually finished, not planned.\n\nThe truly planned experiments are the multi-judge and multi-benchmark formality pairwise comparisons, the Likert versus pairwise sensitivity analysis, the pairwise RATE control, the scaled replication at n=300-500, and the Non-Qwen rewriter control. There are also several completed experiments that could use extension work.\n\nNow I'm checking what the best tier criteria actually require: at least two-thirds of judges need to show significant formality pairwise bias, at least one additional benchmark should replicate the effect, the binarized Likert should remain non-significant across most cells, verbosity scoring needs to complete and show a significant pairwise effect, the RATE control should confirm the original preference stays marginal after multi-judge extension, and direction asymmetry should replicate across judges. I'm also tracking the key metric ranges for the best tier classification. Now I'm looking at the expected ARR score range of 3.5 to 4.0, and mapping out the specific requirements for each experiment—the multi-judge formality test needs at least two-thirds of judges showing significance, the multi-benchmark approach requires replication on at least one additional benchmark like AlpacaEval or MT-Bench, and the Likert sensitivity analysis should demonstrate non-significance across most cells while maintaining strong C2 gap replication rates.\n\nFor the remaining experiments, I'm setting win rate and p-value targets for the scaled n=500 test and the verbosity scoring completion, checking whether the register approach with NLI-only gating could serve as a third validation axis, confirming that non-Qwen rewriter results align with the Qwen baseline to rule out model-specific artifacts, and noting that the kappa=0.43 result from the already-completed experiment is acceptable as a conservative threshold. I should now compile all of this into the YAML output, making sure to include both the fully planned experiments and the partially completed ones that still need finishing.\n\nLooking at what the user actually requested, I need to focus on the experiments marked as \"planned\" in the experiment_plan itself—that's exp-001 through exp-006, exp-009, and exp-013—and provide detailed predictions for each one. I need to stick to the planned experiments the user specified, but I should acknowledge that verbosity completion is part of the best-tier scenario even though exp-007b is technically marked DONE. Let me focus on the seven planned experiments and note where the other factors fit into the narrative, then move on to writing the YAML output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16949,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16949},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51205774-b602-4f29-ade2-87053aa668fb","uuid":"fd511c02-0b14-46fd-898b-7b4357b39035"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Edgeu8wfKicV4RF8pbP6iL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Multi-judge + multi-benchmark generalization confirmed; Likert Blindspot is a robust, general phenomenon.\n  D020 语言修正已到位。实际数据（exp-014 p=0.010, register 95% NLI, binarized Likert p=0.296）比 Dream 2 median 想象更强。\n  Best 档下，Claude/Gemini 复现 formality bias，AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 至少一个复现，\n  verbosity 完成 scoring 成为第二 working axis，binarized Likert 全矩阵非显著 → C2 机制确认。\n  RATE differentiation paragraph 成为最强 positioning argument：RATE 用 Likert ATE，本文证明 Likert 不敏感。\n  Target EMNLP 2026 Main (confident), ARR 预期 3.5–4.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactuals（Qwen3-32B 生成），双向 position-controlled pairwise。\n      GPT-4o 基线：69.1% win rate, p=0.006。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_formality_win_rate: 0.67\n      claude_pairwise_p: 0.012\n      claude_consistent_n: 52\n      claude_formal_wins: 35\n      claude_casual_wins: 17\n      claude_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.76\n      claude_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n      gemini_formality_win_rate: 0.64\n      gemini_pairwise_p: 0.032\n      gemini_consistent_n: 48\n      gemini_formal_wins: 31\n      gemini_casual_wins: 17\n      gemini_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.72\n      gemini_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n      judges_significant_of_3: 3\n      direction_asymmetry_replicated: true\n      position_bias_range: [0.48, 0.55]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 ≥2/3 judges 显著。Formality bias 是 surface-level lexical/syntactic 特征，\n      所有主流 LLM judges 在 RLHF 训练中都暴露于 formal=professional=better 的人类偏好信号，\n      因此 formality preference 是跨模型的系统性偏差而非单一模型 artifact。\n      Claude 略强于 Gemini 的预测基于 Anthropic 模型的 RLHF 训练更注重 professional tone；\n      Gemini Flash 作为轻量模型 bias 可能略弱但仍显著。\n      方向不对称（formal→casual >> casual→formal）跨 judge 复现，因为 formal 版本\n      触发\"更专业\"启发式是 judge 的共性特征，而 casual→formal 方向中 original preference\n      部分抵消了 formality effect（原始文本已足够好，改写为 formal 的边际增益小）。\n      Win rate 在 0.64–0.67 而非更高，因为 n=100 中约 10–15% 的 items 内容差异本身主导判断，\n      style bias 只在其余 items 上表现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Multi-judge formality pairwise results\"\n        columns: [Judge, N_consistent, Formal_wins, Casual_wins, Win_rate, p_value, Direction_F2C, Direction_C2F]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 55, 38, 17, 0.691, 0.006, 0.788, 0.545]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, 52, 35, 17, 0.673, 0.012, 0.760, 0.560]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, 48, 31, 17, 0.646, 0.032, 0.720, 0.540]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: formality win rate by judge with 95% Wilson CI, horizontal line at 50%. All three bars above 0.60, all CIs excluding 0.50.\"\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: formal→casual vs casual→formal win rate by judge. Asymmetry pattern consistent across judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 judges 显著（最强结果），满足 best 档 ≥2/3 要求。方向不对称跨 judge 复现，\n      排除单一模型 artifact 解释。Claude 和 GPT-4o effect size 相近（OR≈2.0–2.2），\n      Gemini 稍弱（OR≈1.8）但仍显著。这为 C1 提供强 multi-judge 支持，\n      并为 RATE differentiation 提供数据：\"如果 RATE 只用 GPT-4o Likert ATE，\n      那 Claude/Gemini 上的 bias 完全被遗漏。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactuals\n      （不同 source texts）。三个 judges（GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini）全部测试。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_win_rate: 0.66\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n      alpacaeval_claude_win_rate: 0.63\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.042\n      alpacaeval_gemini_win_rate: 0.61\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.068\n      mtbench_gpt4o_win_rate: 0.70\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.004\n      mtbench_claude_win_rate: 0.68\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.009\n      mtbench_gemini_win_rate: 0.65\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.028\n      significant_cells_total_9: 7\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.87\n      benchmarks_with_at_least_1_sig: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 ≥1 additional benchmark 复现。MT-Bench 预期效果更强因为其 multi-turn\n      对话格式中 formality 差异更显著（formal 回复在多轮对话中更\"负责任\"）。\n      AlpacaEval 效果稍弱因为其 instruction-following 格式中内容质量权重更高，\n      style bias 的相对贡献被稀释。NLI pass rate 在新 benchmarks 上略低于 LLMBar（0.88），\n      因为 AlpacaEval 的 source texts 更多样化，部分 counterfactual 生成难度更大。\n      9 cells（3 judges × 3 benchmarks）中 7 个显著，2 个边缘（Gemini×AlpacaEval \n      和一个随机 cell 因 n 较小而 power 不足）。这远超 best 档下限 5/9。\n      跨 benchmark 一致性证明 Likert Blindspot 不是 LLMBar 的 artifact。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: 3×3 Judge×Benchmark formality pairwise matrix\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, GPT-4o_WR, GPT-4o_p, Claude_WR, Claude_p, Gemini_WR, Gemini_p]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, 0.691, 0.006, 0.673, 0.012, 0.646, 0.032]\n          - [AlpacaEval, 0.660, 0.018, 0.630, 0.042, 0.610, 0.068]\n          - [MT-Bench, 0.700, 0.004, 0.680, 0.009, 0.650, 0.028]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×3 matrix, color = win rate (blue gradient), asterisks for p<0.05. 7/9 cells starred.\"\n      - \"Forest plot: effect sizes (log OR) with 95% CI across all 9 cells. All point estimates > 0, 7/9 CIs excluding 0.\"\n    analysis: >\n      7/9 cells 显著（p<0.05），远超 best 档要求的 5/9。两个非显著 cell 都是 Gemini×AlpacaEval\n      组合，可解释为 Gemini Flash 在 AlpacaEval 的 open-ended 格式上 bias 表达较弱。\n      MT-Bench > LLMBar > AlpacaEval 的梯度符合 task complexity 假说。\n      关键 takeaway：Likert Blindspot 跨 judges 和 benchmarks 泛化，不是 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 artifact。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark 组合同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate。\n      系统性比较测量敏感度。如果某些 cell 的 Likert 也检测到强效应，\n      则 C2 需限制为 \"Likert fails on weak-to-moderate signals\"。\n    expected_results:\n      likert_significant_cells_of_9: 1\n      pairwise_significant_cells_of_9: 7\n      c2_gap_replication_rate: 0.89\n      likert_ate_range: [-0.15, 0.18]\n      likert_p_range: [0.08, 0.72]\n      pairwise_wr_range: [0.61, 0.70]\n      binarized_likert_significant_cells_of_9: 0\n      binarized_likert_p_range: [0.14, 0.48]\n      one_likert_sig_cell_note: \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench Likert ATE=0.18, p=0.045 — 唯一一个 Likert 接近显著\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 binarized Likert 在 ≥7/9 cells 非显著（实际预测 9/9 非显著）。\n      Likert ATE 在绝大多数 cells 非显著的原因：Likert 的 ordinal scale 压缩了\n      paired comparison 信息，特别是当 bias 幅度在 d=0.1–0.3 范围（如我们的数据），\n      Likert 的 power 远低于 pairwise sign test。这正是 Thurstone 1927 的经典发现\n      在 LLM judge 设定中的复现。唯一可能的 Likert 显著 cell 是 GPT-4o × MT-Bench，\n      因为 MT-Bench 的多轮格式放大了 formality 差异，且 GPT-4o 是 bias 最强的 judge。\n      即便这一个 cell 显著，C2 的表述只需微调为 \"Likert fails for the majority of judge×benchmark \n      combinations\"，不影响核心主张。Binarized Likert 0/9 显著是 C2 最强证据：\n      同样的 sign test，不同的 measurement → gap 来自 measurement structure 而非 test choice。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate vs Binarized Likert across 9 cells\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, Likert_ATE, Likert_p, Pairwise_WR, Pairwise_p, BinLikert_WR, BinLikert_p]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, -0.10, 0.332, 0.691, 0.006, 0.606, 0.296]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, 0.08, 0.420, 0.660, 0.018, 0.580, 0.320]\n          - [GPT-4o, MT-Bench, 0.18, 0.045, 0.700, 0.004, 0.620, 0.140]\n          - [Claude, LLMBar, -0.05, 0.620, 0.673, 0.012, 0.590, 0.280]\n          - [Claude, AlpacaEval, 0.04, 0.710, 0.630, 0.042, 0.560, 0.420]\n          - [Claude, MT-Bench, 0.12, 0.180, 0.680, 0.009, 0.610, 0.180]\n          - [Gemini, LLMBar, -0.08, 0.480, 0.646, 0.032, 0.570, 0.380]\n          - [Gemini, AlpacaEval, 0.02, 0.850, 0.610, 0.068, 0.540, 0.480]\n          - [Gemini, MT-Bench, 0.10, 0.260, 0.650, 0.028, 0.590, 0.260]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: each cell shown as Likert p (red) and Pairwise p (blue) on log scale, horizontal line at p=0.05. Blue dots consistently below line, red dots above.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: Binarized Likert win rate vs Pairwise win rate for all 9 cells. Pairwise consistently 5-10pp higher.\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 gap replication rate 89%（8/9 cells pairwise 显著而 Likert 非显著）。\n      唯一例外 GPT-4o × MT-Bench 的 Likert 勉强显著（p=0.045），可解释为\n      MT-Bench 多轮格式放大 formality 差异到 Likert 勉强可检测的水平。\n      Binarized Likert 9/9 非显著（最低 p=0.140），彻底确认 C2 机制：\n      measurement structure（forced choice vs ordinal rating）是 gap 的原因。\n      论文 headline：\"across 9 judge×benchmark combinations, pairwise detects \n      significant formality bias in 7/9 cells; Likert in 1/9; binarized Likert in 0/9.\"\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite（same style）。\n      量化 original preference confound。必须扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.58\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.56\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.28\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.54\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.45\n      mean_orig_pref_wr_across_9_cells: 0.56\n      cells_with_sig_orig_pref_of_9: 0\n      orig_pref_p_range: [0.08, 0.62]\n      gee_original_pref_OR_multi_judge: 1.65\n      gee_original_pref_p_multi_judge: 0.072\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 original preference 跨 multi-judge 扩展后保持 marginal（p>0.05）。\n      exp-014 已经在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上得到 original preference OR=1.82, p=0.052（marginal）。\n      扩展到 Claude 和 Gemini 后，original preference 预期更弱：Claude 的 RLHF\n      更注重 instruction following 而非文本\"自然度\"，对 double-rewrite 的 penalty 较小；\n      Gemini Flash 作为轻量模型对 subtle 质量差异不敏感。多 judge 汇总的 GEE \n      估计会因异质性而 CI 更宽，p 值更大。0/9 cells 的 original preference 显著，\n      确认 formality bias effect 独立于 original preference confound。\n      如果某个 cell 出现显著的 original preference（比如 GPT-4o × MT-Bench），\n      只要 formality effect 在控制 original preference 后仍显著（如 exp-014 已证明），\n      论文论点不受影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Original preference control across judge×benchmark\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, Orig_Pref_WR, Orig_Pref_p, Formality_WR_controlled, Formality_p_controlled]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, 0.580, 0.180, 0.691, 0.010]\n          - [Claude, LLMBar, 0.560, 0.280, 0.673, 0.015]\n          - [Gemini, LLMBar, 0.540, 0.450, 0.646, 0.038]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired forest plot: formality OR (blue, all significant) vs original preference OR (gray, all non-significant) across 9 cells.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 跨所有 9 cells 非显著，mean win rate 56%（vs formality 66%）。\n      这与 exp-014 的 GEE 结果一致（original OR=1.82 p=0.052）并在 multi-judge 扩展中保持。\n      论文可以自信地声称 formality bias 是 style-driven 而非 original preference artifact。\n      同时为 RATE differentiation 提供弹药：\"RATE 的 Likert ATE 不仅对 style bias 不敏感，\n      其 double-rewrite 控制也可能因 original preference 的 marginal confound 而不纯净。\"\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 primary formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。在 best-performing judge × benchmark\n      组合上运行。包含 power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n: 500\n      judge: \"GPT-4o\"\n      benchmark: \"MT-Bench\"\n      n_consistent: 280\n      formal_wins: 194\n      casual_wins: 86\n      win_rate: 0.693\n      sign_test_p: 0.00001\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.637\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.744\n      formal_to_casual_wr: 0.78\n      casual_to_formal_wr: 0.56\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      power_at_d02: 0.92\n      power_at_d015: 0.78\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.09\n      likert_p_n500: 0.082\n      binarized_likert_p_n500: 0.065\n      cohens_h: 0.39\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 n=500 formality win rate 在 0.63–0.72, p 在 0.0001–0.005。\n      预测 win rate 0.693 与 n=100 的 0.691 高度一致，因为 formality bias 是稳定的\n      系统性偏差，不会因样本量变化而改变 effect size。p 值从 0.006 降到 0.00001\n      纯粹是 power 增加的结果。关键增值：CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.64, 0.74]，\n      精确量化 bias 幅度。Likert 在 n=500 仍然非显著（p=0.082），尽管比 n=100\n      的 p=0.332 有所降低——这说明 Likert 在极大样本下可能最终检测到 bias，\n      但所需样本量是 pairwise 的 5–10 倍，进一步支持 C2。\n      Binarized Likert p=0.065 在 n=500 下接近边缘，这是一个微妙结果：\n      说明 binarized Likert 的 power 介于 raw Likert 和 pairwise 之间，\n      但 forced binary 后的信息仍不如真正的 pairwise comparison 因为 binarized \n      仍基于独立评分而非直接比较。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Scaled replication results\"\n        columns: [Metric, n_100, n_500]\n        rows:\n          - [Win_rate, 0.691, 0.693]\n          - [p_value, 0.006, 0.00001]\n          - [Wilson_CI_width, 0.238, 0.107]\n          - [Formal_to_casual_WR, 0.788, 0.780]\n          - [Casual_to_formal_WR, 0.545, 0.560]\n          - [Likert_p, 0.332, 0.082]\n          - [BinLikert_p, 0.296, 0.065]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accumulation curve: win rate (y-axis) vs sample size (x-axis, 50 to 500 in increments of 50). Shows stability of effect around 0.69 with narrowing CI ribbon.\"\n      - \"Power curve: statistical power vs effect size for pairwise (blue), binarized Likert (orange), raw Likert (red). Pairwise reaches 80% power at d=0.15, Likert at d=0.35.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Effect size 在 n=500 完美复现（0.693 vs 0.691），确认 formality bias 是\n      robust systematic effect 而非 small-sample fluke。Power analysis 量化了\n      Likert Blindspot 的 practical cost：检测 d=0.2 的 style bias，pairwise 需 n≈80，\n      Likert 需 n≈400+。这为 practitioner guidance 提供定量基础。\n      Direction asymmetry 在大样本下保持，排除了小样本波动解释。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用非 Qwen 模型（Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen 家族 artifact。\n      比较 NLI pass rate 和 pairwise 结果。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      llama_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.78\n      llama_both_pass_rate: 0.72\n      llama_pairwise_consistent_n: 50\n      llama_formal_wins: 33\n      llama_casual_wins: 17\n      llama_win_rate: 0.66\n      llama_p: 0.022\n      qwen_vs_llama_wr_diff: 0.03\n      qwen_vs_llama_wr_diff_p: 0.68\n      nli_pass_rate_diff: 0.04\n      direction_asymmetry_preserved: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B 已产出 NLI 88% pass rate 的高质量 counterfactuals。Llama-3.1-70B\n      作为不同架构、不同训练数据的模型，counterfactual 质量预期略低（84% NLI pass）\n      因为 Qwen 在中文和指令遵循上更强（虽然任务是英文，但 Qwen3 的 instruction tuning\n      更精细）。关键是 pairwise 结果（0.66 vs 0.69）无统计显著差异（p=0.68），\n      确认 formality bias 检测不依赖特定 rewriter。Win rate 略低可能因为\n      Llama 的 counterfactuals 在 style transfer 力度上稍弱（更保守的改写），\n      但方向和显著性不变。Direction asymmetry 保持，因为这是 judge 端属性\n      而非 rewriter 端属性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Rewriter comparison\"\n        columns: [Metric, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B, Diff_p]\n        rows:\n          - [NLI_pass_rate, 0.88, 0.84, 0.42]\n          - [Pairwise_WR, 0.691, 0.660, 0.68]\n          - [Pairwise_p, 0.006, 0.022, \"-\"]\n          - [F2C_WR, 0.788, 0.750, 0.55]\n          - [C2F_WR, 0.545, 0.540, 0.92]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side bar charts: Qwen vs Llama win rates with CIs. Overlapping CIs confirm no rewriter effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter 无显著影响（差异 3pp, p=0.68），排除 Qwen artifact。\n      这是一个必要但不 exciting 的 robustness check。论文用一段报告即可。\n      实际意义：practitioners 可以用任何高质量 LLM 作为 rewriter，不被 Qwen 绑定。\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human 标注 NLI gate decisions。100 pairs，报告 Cohen's kappa。\n      已完成：kappa=0.43, agreement 91%, FP rate 1.1%, FN rate 66.7%。\n      Best 档将 kappa=0.43 定位为 conservative gate → lower-bound estimate。\n    expected_results:\n      kappa: 0.4304\n      agreement_rate: 0.91\n      false_positive_rate: 0.0114\n      false_negative_rate: 0.6667\n      n_samples: 100\n      tp: 87\n      fp: 1\n      fn: 8\n      tn: 4\n      framing: \"conservative gate yielding lower-bound bias estimates\"\n      additional_analysis_pass_rate_at_0.80: 0.93\n      additional_analysis_pass_rate_at_0.85: 0.91\n    result_rationale: >\n      Kappa=0.43 表面上是 \"moderate agreement\"，但分布极度不平衡（91% pass）导致\n      kappa 被 base rate 压低（prevalence-adjusted kappa 更高）。关键是 FP rate 1.1%：\n      NLI 几乎不会把 content-changing pairs 误判为 content-preserving，因此通过 NLI gate\n      的 pairs 几乎肯定是 valid counterfactuals。FN rate 67% 高但方向正确——NLI gate\n      是保守的，丢弃了一些人类认为 OK 的 pairs，这只降低 power（需要更多样本才能\n      检测效果）但不引入 false discovery。论文表述：\"NLI gate operates as a conservative \n      filter (FP=1.1%) — our reported bias magnitudes are lower-bound estimates; \n      the true effect, inclusive of NLI-rejected but human-valid pairs, is likely larger.\"\n      这把 kappa 的 apparent weakness 转化为 methodological strength。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Human-NLI agreement confusion matrix\"\n        columns: [\" \", NLI_Pass, NLI_Fail]\n        rows:\n          - [Human_Pass, \"TP=87\", \"FN=8\"]\n          - [Human_Fail, \"FP=1\", \"TN=4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap with counts and rates. FP cell highlighted in green (1.1%) to emphasize conservative gating.\"\n    analysis: >\n      FP rate 1.1% 是最有力的数字。论文强调 NLI gate 的 precision（87/88 = 98.9%），\n      而非 recall。Reviewer 若质疑 kappa=0.43，response letter 指出 prevalence paradox\n      和 FP=1.1% → lower-bound framing。如果 reviewer 仍不满意，可以报告\n      \"bias results on the n=87 human-validated subset\" 作为 robustness check——\n      win rate 只会更高（因为 NLI gate 丢弃的是偏 ambiguous 的 pairs）。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity full pipeline completion\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007b\"\n    description: >\n      Verbosity H1 PASS（direction-aware NLI 86%）后 scoring 被 API 402 阻断。\n      API 恢复后完成 scoring + pairwise + ATE pipeline。\n      Best 档要求 verbosity 成为第二 working axis。\n    expected_results:\n      n_nli_pass: 86\n      n_consistent: 45\n      verbose_wins: 30\n      concise_wins: 15\n      verbose_win_rate: 0.667\n      pairwise_p: 0.024\n      verbose_to_concise_wr: 0.72\n      concise_to_verbose_wr: 0.58\n      likert_ate: 0.15\n      likert_p: 0.18\n      binarized_likert_p: 0.22\n      direction_aware_nli_benefit: \"+21pp over bidirectional (86% vs 65%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 verbosity pairwise win rate 0.60–0.72, p 0.005–0.045。\n      Verbosity bias 在 LLM judges 中有充分文献支持（LC-AlpacaEval 整篇论文都在处理 length bias，\n      SOS-Bench R=0.999）。Direction-aware NLI 解决了 v1 的 bidirectional NLI 瓶颈后，\n      86% 的 valid counterfactuals 提供了足够 power。Win rate 0.667 略低于 formality（0.691），\n      因为 verbosity 更容易被 content quality 混淆（verbose 版本可能包含更多信息，\n      不纯粹是 style），且 direction-aware NLI gate 可能遗漏了一些 content-adding cases。\n      Likert 仍然非显著（p=0.18），复现 C2 pattern。这是最有价值的实验之一：\n      第二 axis 把论文从 \"formality case study\" 升级为 \"generalizable phenomenon\"。\n      Direction-aware NLI 本身就是方法论贡献——处理 information-changing axes 的通用方案。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Verbosity pairwise results\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [N_valid_NLI, 86]\n          - [N_consistent, 45]\n          - [Verbose_wins, 30]\n          - [Concise_wins, 15]\n          - [Win_rate, 0.667]\n          - [p_value, 0.024]\n          - [Likert_p, 0.180]\n          - [BinLikert_p, 0.220]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: formality and verbosity win rates side by side, both above 0.60, both with Likert p > 0.05. Visual evidence of C2 generalization.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 成为第二 working axis（n_working_axes=2），满足 best 档要求。\n      C2 Likert Blindspot 在两个 axes 上复现。C3 从 \"preliminary with one axis\" 升级为\n      \"two confirmed axes + one negative control (tone) + one pending (register)\"。\n      Direction-aware NLI 作为方法论贡献写入 Method 节，增强论文 novelty。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis n=100 completion\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Register pilot NLI-only 95% PASS。生成 n=100 counterfactuals 并完成 scoring pipeline。\n      使用 NLI-only gate（BERTScore 是 sole bottleneck，0.92 threshold 不适用于 register）。\n    expected_results:\n      n_generated: 100\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.91\n      n_nli_pass: 91\n      n_consistent: 48\n      academic_wins: 30\n      conversational_wins: 18\n      academic_win_rate: 0.625\n      pairwise_p: 0.068\n      register_formality_agreement: 0.52\n      direction_asymmetry: \"academic→conversational 0.70 vs conversational→academic 0.52\"\n      likert_p: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register 在 best 档下是 potential third axis 但预测为 marginal（p=0.068）。\n      Register（academic vs conversational）与 formality 50% 正交，说明测量的是\n      不同维度。Academic register 的 bias 预期弱于 formality 因为：(1) register \n      变化涉及更多词汇替换（jargon、句法结构），NLI gate 可能丢弃更多 valid pairs；\n      (2) academic register 不像 formal tone 那样有统一的\"更好\"启发式——\n      有些 context 中 conversational 更合适（如 chatbot 评估）。\n      即便 p=0.068 不显著，register 作为\"第三 axis，方向一致但 power 不足\"\n      仍支持 C3 的 \"preliminary evidence\" framing，且与 n_working_axes=2-3 的\n      best 档范围一致（如果 register 显著则 n=3，不显著则 n=2）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Register pairwise results\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [N_NLI_pass, 91]\n          - [N_consistent, 48]\n          - [Academic_wins, 30]\n          - [Win_rate, 0.625]\n          - [p_value, 0.068]\n          - [Likert_p, 0.420]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Summary bar chart: all axes (formality, verbosity, register, tone) win rates. Formality and verbosity above 0.05 sig line, register marginal, tone flat.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register marginal significance 对论文有两种 spinning：\n      (1) 如果 p<0.05，第三 working axis，C3 大幅强化；\n      (2) 如果 p=0.068，\"suggestive evidence consistent with C3, power-limited at n=100\"，\n      仍支持 \"axis-dependent sensitivity\" narrative。Either way，论文不受损。\n      NLI-only gate 的成功（0.91 vs joint 0.20）本身支持 \"BERTScore \n      is an unnecessarily strict bottleneck for vocabulary-changing axes\" 这一方法论发现。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16949,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16949},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51205774-b602-4f29-ade2-87053aa668fb","uuid":"57727b37-f592-4dbf-9e8a-da56e93ce3fa"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":229952,"duration_api_ms":232110,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Multi-judge + multi-benchmark generalization confirmed; Likert Blindspot is a robust, general phenomenon.\n  D020 语言修正已到位。实际数据（exp-014 p=0.010, register 95% NLI, binarized Likert p=0.296）比 Dream 2 median 想象更强。\n  Best 档下，Claude/Gemini 复现 formality bias，AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 至少一个复现，\n  verbosity 完成 scoring 成为第二 working axis，binarized Likert 全矩阵非显著 → C2 机制确认。\n  RATE differentiation paragraph 成为最强 positioning argument：RATE 用 Likert ATE，本文证明 Likert 不敏感。\n  Target EMNLP 2026 Main (confident), ARR 预期 3.5–4.0。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复现 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactuals（Qwen3-32B 生成），双向 position-controlled pairwise。\n      GPT-4o 基线：69.1% win rate, p=0.006。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_formality_win_rate: 0.67\n      claude_pairwise_p: 0.012\n      claude_consistent_n: 52\n      claude_formal_wins: 35\n      claude_casual_wins: 17\n      claude_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.76\n      claude_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n      gemini_formality_win_rate: 0.64\n      gemini_pairwise_p: 0.032\n      gemini_consistent_n: 48\n      gemini_formal_wins: 31\n      gemini_casual_wins: 17\n      gemini_formal_to_casual_win_rate: 0.72\n      gemini_casual_to_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n      judges_significant_of_3: 3\n      direction_asymmetry_replicated: true\n      position_bias_range: [0.48, 0.55]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 ≥2/3 judges 显著。Formality bias 是 surface-level lexical/syntactic 特征，\n      所有主流 LLM judges 在 RLHF 训练中都暴露于 formal=professional=better 的人类偏好信号，\n      因此 formality preference 是跨模型的系统性偏差而非单一模型 artifact。\n      Claude 略强于 Gemini 的预测基于 Anthropic 模型的 RLHF 训练更注重 professional tone；\n      Gemini Flash 作为轻量模型 bias 可能略弱但仍显著。\n      方向不对称（formal→casual >> casual→formal）跨 judge 复现，因为 formal 版本\n      触发\"更专业\"启发式是 judge 的共性特征，而 casual→formal 方向中 original preference\n      部分抵消了 formality effect（原始文本已足够好，改写为 formal 的边际增益小）。\n      Win rate 在 0.64–0.67 而非更高，因为 n=100 中约 10–15% 的 items 内容差异本身主导判断，\n      style bias 只在其余 items 上表现。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Multi-judge formality pairwise results\"\n        columns: [Judge, N_consistent, Formal_wins, Casual_wins, Win_rate, p_value, Direction_F2C, Direction_C2F]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, 55, 38, 17, 0.691, 0.006, 0.788, 0.545]\n          - [Claude-Sonnet, 52, 35, 17, 0.673, 0.012, 0.760, 0.560]\n          - [Gemini-Flash, 48, 31, 17, 0.646, 0.032, 0.720, 0.540]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: formality win rate by judge with 95% Wilson CI, horizontal line at 50%. All three bars above 0.60, all CIs excluding 0.50.\"\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: formal→casual vs casual→formal win rate by judge. Asymmetry pattern consistent across judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      3/3 judges 显著（最强结果），满足 best 档 ≥2/3 要求。方向不对称跨 judge 复现，\n      排除单一模型 artifact 解释。Claude 和 GPT-4o effect size 相近（OR≈2.0–2.2），\n      Gemini 稍弱（OR≈1.8）但仍显著。这为 C1 提供强 multi-judge 支持，\n      并为 RATE differentiation 提供数据：\"如果 RATE 只用 GPT-4o Likert ATE，\n      那 Claude/Gemini 上的 bias 完全被遗漏。\"\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 子集上运行 CSD pipeline。需要新生成 counterfactuals\n      （不同 source texts）。三个 judges（GPT-4o + Claude + Gemini）全部测试。\n    expected_results:\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_win_rate: 0.66\n      alpacaeval_gpt4o_p: 0.018\n      alpacaeval_claude_win_rate: 0.63\n      alpacaeval_claude_p: 0.042\n      alpacaeval_gemini_win_rate: 0.61\n      alpacaeval_gemini_p: 0.068\n      mtbench_gpt4o_win_rate: 0.70\n      mtbench_gpt4o_p: 0.004\n      mtbench_claude_win_rate: 0.68\n      mtbench_claude_p: 0.009\n      mtbench_gemini_win_rate: 0.65\n      mtbench_gemini_p: 0.028\n      significant_cells_total_9: 7\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.87\n      benchmarks_with_at_least_1_sig: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 ≥1 additional benchmark 复现。MT-Bench 预期效果更强因为其 multi-turn\n      对话格式中 formality 差异更显著（formal 回复在多轮对话中更\"负责任\"）。\n      AlpacaEval 效果稍弱因为其 instruction-following 格式中内容质量权重更高，\n      style bias 的相对贡献被稀释。NLI pass rate 在新 benchmarks 上略低于 LLMBar（0.88），\n      因为 AlpacaEval 的 source texts 更多样化，部分 counterfactual 生成难度更大。\n      9 cells（3 judges × 3 benchmarks）中 7 个显著，2 个边缘（Gemini×AlpacaEval \n      和一个随机 cell 因 n 较小而 power 不足）。这远超 best 档下限 5/9。\n      跨 benchmark 一致性证明 Likert Blindspot 不是 LLMBar 的 artifact。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: 3×3 Judge×Benchmark formality pairwise matrix\"\n        columns: [Benchmark, GPT-4o_WR, GPT-4o_p, Claude_WR, Claude_p, Gemini_WR, Gemini_p]\n        rows:\n          - [LLMBar, 0.691, 0.006, 0.673, 0.012, 0.646, 0.032]\n          - [AlpacaEval, 0.660, 0.018, 0.630, 0.042, 0.610, 0.068]\n          - [MT-Bench, 0.700, 0.004, 0.680, 0.009, 0.650, 0.028]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×3 matrix, color = win rate (blue gradient), asterisks for p<0.05. 7/9 cells starred.\"\n      - \"Forest plot: effect sizes (log OR) with 95% CI across all 9 cells. All point estimates > 0, 7/9 CIs excluding 0.\"\n    analysis: >\n      7/9 cells 显著（p<0.05），远超 best 档要求的 5/9。两个非显著 cell 都是 Gemini×AlpacaEval\n      组合，可解释为 Gemini Flash 在 AlpacaEval 的 open-ended 格式上 bias 表达较弱。\n      MT-Bench > LLMBar > AlpacaEval 的梯度符合 task complexity 假说。\n      关键 takeaway：Likert Blindspot 跨 judges 和 benchmarks 泛化，不是 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 artifact。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark 组合同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate。\n      系统性比较测量敏感度。如果某些 cell 的 Likert 也检测到强效应，\n      则 C2 需限制为 \"Likert fails on weak-to-moderate signals\"。\n    expected_results:\n      likert_significant_cells_of_9: 1\n      pairwise_significant_cells_of_9: 7\n      c2_gap_replication_rate: 0.89\n      likert_ate_range: [-0.15, 0.18]\n      likert_p_range: [0.08, 0.72]\n      pairwise_wr_range: [0.61, 0.70]\n      binarized_likert_significant_cells_of_9: 0\n      binarized_likert_p_range: [0.14, 0.48]\n      one_likert_sig_cell_note: \"GPT-4o × MT-Bench Likert ATE=0.18, p=0.045 — 唯一一个 Likert 接近显著\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 binarized Likert 在 ≥7/9 cells 非显著（实际预测 9/9 非显著）。\n      Likert ATE 在绝大多数 cells 非显著的原因：Likert 的 ordinal scale 压缩了\n      paired comparison 信息，特别是当 bias 幅度在 d=0.1–0.3 范围（如我们的数据），\n      Likert 的 power 远低于 pairwise sign test。这正是 Thurstone 1927 的经典发现\n      在 LLM judge 设定中的复现。唯一可能的 Likert 显著 cell 是 GPT-4o × MT-Bench，\n      因为 MT-Bench 的多轮格式放大了 formality 差异，且 GPT-4o 是 bias 最强的 judge。\n      即便这一个 cell 显著，C2 的表述只需微调为 \"Likert fails for the majority of judge×benchmark \n      combinations\"，不影响核心主张。Binarized Likert 0/9 显著是 C2 最强证据：\n      同样的 sign test，不同的 measurement → gap 来自 measurement structure 而非 test choice。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Likert ATE vs Pairwise Win Rate vs Binarized Likert across 9 cells\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, Likert_ATE, Likert_p, Pairwise_WR, Pairwise_p, BinLikert_WR, BinLikert_p]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, -0.10, 0.332, 0.691, 0.006, 0.606, 0.296]\n          - [GPT-4o, AlpacaEval, 0.08, 0.420, 0.660, 0.018, 0.580, 0.320]\n          - [GPT-4o, MT-Bench, 0.18, 0.045, 0.700, 0.004, 0.620, 0.140]\n          - [Claude, LLMBar, -0.05, 0.620, 0.673, 0.012, 0.590, 0.280]\n          - [Claude, AlpacaEval, 0.04, 0.710, 0.630, 0.042, 0.560, 0.420]\n          - [Claude, MT-Bench, 0.12, 0.180, 0.680, 0.009, 0.610, 0.180]\n          - [Gemini, LLMBar, -0.08, 0.480, 0.646, 0.032, 0.570, 0.380]\n          - [Gemini, AlpacaEval, 0.02, 0.850, 0.610, 0.068, 0.540, 0.480]\n          - [Gemini, MT-Bench, 0.10, 0.260, 0.650, 0.028, 0.590, 0.260]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired dot plot: each cell shown as Likert p (red) and Pairwise p (blue) on log scale, horizontal line at p=0.05. Blue dots consistently below line, red dots above.\"\n      - \"Bar chart: Binarized Likert win rate vs Pairwise win rate for all 9 cells. Pairwise consistently 5-10pp higher.\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 gap replication rate 89%（8/9 cells pairwise 显著而 Likert 非显著）。\n      唯一例外 GPT-4o × MT-Bench 的 Likert 勉强显著（p=0.045），可解释为\n      MT-Bench 多轮格式放大 formality 差异到 Likert 勉强可检测的水平。\n      Binarized Likert 9/9 非显著（最低 p=0.140），彻底确认 C2 机制：\n      measurement structure（forced choice vs ordinal rating）是 gap 的原因。\n      论文 headline：\"across 9 judge×benchmark combinations, pairwise detects \n      significant formality bias in 7/9 cells; Likert in 1/9; binarized Likert in 0/9.\"\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise comparison between original text 和 RATE double-rewrite（same style）。\n      量化 original preference confound。必须扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.58\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.56\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.28\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.54\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.45\n      mean_orig_pref_wr_across_9_cells: 0.56\n      cells_with_sig_orig_pref_of_9: 0\n      orig_pref_p_range: [0.08, 0.62]\n      gee_original_pref_OR_multi_judge: 1.65\n      gee_original_pref_p_multi_judge: 0.072\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 original preference 跨 multi-judge 扩展后保持 marginal（p>0.05）。\n      exp-014 已经在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上得到 original preference OR=1.82, p=0.052（marginal）。\n      扩展到 Claude 和 Gemini 后，original preference 预期更弱：Claude 的 RLHF\n      更注重 instruction following 而非文本\"自然度\"，对 double-rewrite 的 penalty 较小；\n      Gemini Flash 作为轻量模型对 subtle 质量差异不敏感。多 judge 汇总的 GEE \n      估计会因异质性而 CI 更宽，p 值更大。0/9 cells 的 original preference 显著，\n      确认 formality bias effect 独立于 original preference confound。\n      如果某个 cell 出现显著的 original preference（比如 GPT-4o × MT-Bench），\n      只要 formality effect 在控制 original preference 后仍显著（如 exp-014 已证明），\n      论文论点不受影响。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Original preference control across judge×benchmark\"\n        columns: [Judge, Benchmark, Orig_Pref_WR, Orig_Pref_p, Formality_WR_controlled, Formality_p_controlled]\n        rows:\n          - [GPT-4o, LLMBar, 0.580, 0.180, 0.691, 0.010]\n          - [Claude, LLMBar, 0.560, 0.280, 0.673, 0.015]\n          - [Gemini, LLMBar, 0.540, 0.450, 0.646, 0.038]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired forest plot: formality OR (blue, all significant) vs original preference OR (gray, all non-significant) across 9 cells.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 跨所有 9 cells 非显著，mean win rate 56%（vs formality 66%）。\n      这与 exp-014 的 GEE 结果一致（original OR=1.82 p=0.052）并在 multi-judge 扩展中保持。\n      论文可以自信地声称 formality bias 是 style-driven 而非 original preference artifact。\n      同时为 RATE differentiation 提供弹药：\"RATE 的 Likert ATE 不仅对 style bias 不敏感，\n      其 double-rewrite 控制也可能因 original preference 的 marginal confound 而不纯净。\"\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 primary formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=500。在 best-performing judge × benchmark\n      组合上运行。包含 power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n: 500\n      judge: \"GPT-4o\"\n      benchmark: \"MT-Bench\"\n      n_consistent: 280\n      formal_wins: 194\n      casual_wins: 86\n      win_rate: 0.693\n      sign_test_p: 0.00001\n      wilson_ci_lo: 0.637\n      wilson_ci_hi: 0.744\n      formal_to_casual_wr: 0.78\n      casual_to_formal_wr: 0.56\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.86\n      power_at_d02: 0.92\n      power_at_d015: 0.78\n      likert_ate_n500: 0.09\n      likert_p_n500: 0.082\n      binarized_likert_p_n500: 0.065\n      cohens_h: 0.39\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 n=500 formality win rate 在 0.63–0.72, p 在 0.0001–0.005。\n      预测 win rate 0.693 与 n=100 的 0.691 高度一致，因为 formality bias 是稳定的\n      系统性偏差，不会因样本量变化而改变 effect size。p 值从 0.006 降到 0.00001\n      纯粹是 power 增加的结果。关键增值：CI 从 [0.56, 0.80] 收窄到 [0.64, 0.74]，\n      精确量化 bias 幅度。Likert 在 n=500 仍然非显著（p=0.082），尽管比 n=100\n      的 p=0.332 有所降低——这说明 Likert 在极大样本下可能最终检测到 bias，\n      但所需样本量是 pairwise 的 5–10 倍，进一步支持 C2。\n      Binarized Likert p=0.065 在 n=500 下接近边缘，这是一个微妙结果：\n      说明 binarized Likert 的 power 介于 raw Likert 和 pairwise 之间，\n      但 forced binary 后的信息仍不如真正的 pairwise comparison 因为 binarized \n      仍基于独立评分而非直接比较。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Scaled replication results\"\n        columns: [Metric, n_100, n_500]\n        rows:\n          - [Win_rate, 0.691, 0.693]\n          - [p_value, 0.006, 0.00001]\n          - [Wilson_CI_width, 0.238, 0.107]\n          - [Formal_to_casual_WR, 0.788, 0.780]\n          - [Casual_to_formal_WR, 0.545, 0.560]\n          - [Likert_p, 0.332, 0.082]\n          - [BinLikert_p, 0.296, 0.065]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Accumulation curve: win rate (y-axis) vs sample size (x-axis, 50 to 500 in increments of 50). Shows stability of effect around 0.69 with narrowing CI ribbon.\"\n      - \"Power curve: statistical power vs effect size for pairwise (blue), binarized Likert (orange), raw Likert (red). Pairwise reaches 80% power at d=0.15, Likert at d=0.35.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Effect size 在 n=500 完美复现（0.693 vs 0.691），确认 formality bias 是\n      robust systematic effect 而非 small-sample fluke。Power analysis 量化了\n      Likert Blindspot 的 practical cost：检测 d=0.2 的 style bias，pairwise 需 n≈80，\n      Likert 需 n≈400+。这为 practitioner guidance 提供定量基础。\n      Direction asymmetry 在大样本下保持，排除了小样本波动解释。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用非 Qwen 模型（Llama-3.1-70B）作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen 家族 artifact。\n      比较 NLI pass rate 和 pairwise 结果。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.84\n      llama_bertscore_pass_rate: 0.78\n      llama_both_pass_rate: 0.72\n      llama_pairwise_consistent_n: 50\n      llama_formal_wins: 33\n      llama_casual_wins: 17\n      llama_win_rate: 0.66\n      llama_p: 0.022\n      qwen_vs_llama_wr_diff: 0.03\n      qwen_vs_llama_wr_diff_p: 0.68\n      nli_pass_rate_diff: 0.04\n      direction_asymmetry_preserved: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-32B 已产出 NLI 88% pass rate 的高质量 counterfactuals。Llama-3.1-70B\n      作为不同架构、不同训练数据的模型，counterfactual 质量预期略低（84% NLI pass）\n      因为 Qwen 在中文和指令遵循上更强（虽然任务是英文，但 Qwen3 的 instruction tuning\n      更精细）。关键是 pairwise 结果（0.66 vs 0.69）无统计显著差异（p=0.68），\n      确认 formality bias 检测不依赖特定 rewriter。Win rate 略低可能因为\n      Llama 的 counterfactuals 在 style transfer 力度上稍弱（更保守的改写），\n      但方向和显著性不变。Direction asymmetry 保持，因为这是 judge 端属性\n      而非 rewriter 端属性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Rewriter comparison\"\n        columns: [Metric, Qwen3-32B, Llama-3.1-70B, Diff_p]\n        rows:\n          - [NLI_pass_rate, 0.88, 0.84, 0.42]\n          - [Pairwise_WR, 0.691, 0.660, 0.68]\n          - [Pairwise_p, 0.006, 0.022, \"-\"]\n          - [F2C_WR, 0.788, 0.750, 0.55]\n          - [C2F_WR, 0.545, 0.540, 0.92]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Side-by-side bar charts: Qwen vs Llama win rates with CIs. Overlapping CIs confirm no rewriter effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Rewriter 无显著影响（差异 3pp, p=0.68），排除 Qwen artifact。\n      这是一个必要但不 exciting 的 robustness check。论文用一段报告即可。\n      实际意义：practitioners 可以用任何高质量 LLM 作为 rewriter，不被 Qwen 绑定。\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      Human 标注 NLI gate decisions。100 pairs，报告 Cohen's kappa。\n      已完成：kappa=0.43, agreement 91%, FP rate 1.1%, FN rate 66.7%。\n      Best 档将 kappa=0.43 定位为 conservative gate → lower-bound estimate。\n    expected_results:\n      kappa: 0.4304\n      agreement_rate: 0.91\n      false_positive_rate: 0.0114\n      false_negative_rate: 0.6667\n      n_samples: 100\n      tp: 87\n      fp: 1\n      fn: 8\n      tn: 4\n      framing: \"conservative gate yielding lower-bound bias estimates\"\n      additional_analysis_pass_rate_at_0.80: 0.93\n      additional_analysis_pass_rate_at_0.85: 0.91\n    result_rationale: >\n      Kappa=0.43 表面上是 \"moderate agreement\"，但分布极度不平衡（91% pass）导致\n      kappa 被 base rate 压低（prevalence-adjusted kappa 更高）。关键是 FP rate 1.1%：\n      NLI 几乎不会把 content-changing pairs 误判为 content-preserving，因此通过 NLI gate\n      的 pairs 几乎肯定是 valid counterfactuals。FN rate 67% 高但方向正确——NLI gate\n      是保守的，丢弃了一些人类认为 OK 的 pairs，这只降低 power（需要更多样本才能\n      检测效果）但不引入 false discovery。论文表述：\"NLI gate operates as a conservative \n      filter (FP=1.1%) — our reported bias magnitudes are lower-bound estimates; \n      the true effect, inclusive of NLI-rejected but human-valid pairs, is likely larger.\"\n      这把 kappa 的 apparent weakness 转化为 methodological strength。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Human-NLI agreement confusion matrix\"\n        columns: [\" \", NLI_Pass, NLI_Fail]\n        rows:\n          - [Human_Pass, \"TP=87\", \"FN=8\"]\n          - [Human_Fail, \"FP=1\", \"TN=4\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap with counts and rates. FP cell highlighted in green (1.1%) to emphasize conservative gating.\"\n    analysis: >\n      FP rate 1.1% 是最有力的数字。论文强调 NLI gate 的 precision（87/88 = 98.9%），\n      而非 recall。Reviewer 若质疑 kappa=0.43，response letter 指出 prevalence paradox\n      和 FP=1.1% → lower-bound framing。如果 reviewer 仍不满意，可以报告\n      \"bias results on the n=87 human-validated subset\" 作为 robustness check——\n      win rate 只会更高（因为 NLI gate 丢弃的是偏 ambiguous 的 pairs）。\n\n  - name: \"Verbosity full pipeline completion\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-007b\"\n    description: >\n      Verbosity H1 PASS（direction-aware NLI 86%）后 scoring 被 API 402 阻断。\n      API 恢复后完成 scoring + pairwise + ATE pipeline。\n      Best 档要求 verbosity 成为第二 working axis。\n    expected_results:\n      n_nli_pass: 86\n      n_consistent: 45\n      verbose_wins: 30\n      concise_wins: 15\n      verbose_win_rate: 0.667\n      pairwise_p: 0.024\n      verbose_to_concise_wr: 0.72\n      concise_to_verbose_wr: 0.58\n      likert_ate: 0.15\n      likert_p: 0.18\n      binarized_likert_p: 0.22\n      direction_aware_nli_benefit: \"+21pp over bidirectional (86% vs 65%)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档要求 verbosity pairwise win rate 0.60–0.72, p 0.005–0.045。\n      Verbosity bias 在 LLM judges 中有充分文献支持（LC-AlpacaEval 整篇论文都在处理 length bias，\n      SOS-Bench R=0.999）。Direction-aware NLI 解决了 v1 的 bidirectional NLI 瓶颈后，\n      86% 的 valid counterfactuals 提供了足够 power。Win rate 0.667 略低于 formality（0.691），\n      因为 verbosity 更容易被 content quality 混淆（verbose 版本可能包含更多信息，\n      不纯粹是 style），且 direction-aware NLI gate 可能遗漏了一些 content-adding cases。\n      Likert 仍然非显著（p=0.18），复现 C2 pattern。这是最有价值的实验之一：\n      第二 axis 把论文从 \"formality case study\" 升级为 \"generalizable phenomenon\"。\n      Direction-aware NLI 本身就是方法论贡献——处理 information-changing axes 的通用方案。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Verbosity pairwise results\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [N_valid_NLI, 86]\n          - [N_consistent, 45]\n          - [Verbose_wins, 30]\n          - [Concise_wins, 15]\n          - [Win_rate, 0.667]\n          - [p_value, 0.024]\n          - [Likert_p, 0.180]\n          - [BinLikert_p, 0.220]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: formality and verbosity win rates side by side, both above 0.60, both with Likert p > 0.05. Visual evidence of C2 generalization.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Verbosity 成为第二 working axis（n_working_axes=2），满足 best 档要求。\n      C2 Likert Blindspot 在两个 axes 上复现。C3 从 \"preliminary with one axis\" 升级为\n      \"two confirmed axes + one negative control (tone) + one pending (register)\"。\n      Direction-aware NLI 作为方法论贡献写入 Method 节，增强论文 novelty。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis n=100 completion\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      Register pilot NLI-only 95% PASS。生成 n=100 counterfactuals 并完成 scoring pipeline。\n      使用 NLI-only gate（BERTScore 是 sole bottleneck，0.92 threshold 不适用于 register）。\n    expected_results:\n      n_generated: 100\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.91\n      n_nli_pass: 91\n      n_consistent: 48\n      academic_wins: 30\n      conversational_wins: 18\n      academic_win_rate: 0.625\n      pairwise_p: 0.068\n      register_formality_agreement: 0.52\n      direction_asymmetry: \"academic→conversational 0.70 vs conversational→academic 0.52\"\n      likert_p: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      Register 在 best 档下是 potential third axis 但预测为 marginal（p=0.068）。\n      Register（academic vs conversational）与 formality 50% 正交，说明测量的是\n      不同维度。Academic register 的 bias 预期弱于 formality 因为：(1) register \n      变化涉及更多词汇替换（jargon、句法结构），NLI gate 可能丢弃更多 valid pairs；\n      (2) academic register 不像 formal tone 那样有统一的\"更好\"启发式——\n      有些 context 中 conversational 更合适（如 chatbot 评估）。\n      即便 p=0.068 不显著，register 作为\"第三 axis，方向一致但 power 不足\"\n      仍支持 C3 的 \"preliminary evidence\" framing，且与 n_working_axes=2-3 的\n      best 档范围一致（如果 register 显著则 n=3，不显著则 n=2）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Register pairwise results\"\n        columns: [Metric, Value]\n        rows:\n          - [N_NLI_pass, 91]\n          - [N_consistent, 48]\n          - [Academic_wins, 30]\n          - [Win_rate, 0.625]\n          - [p_value, 0.068]\n          - [Likert_p, 0.420]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Summary bar chart: all axes (formality, verbosity, register, tone) win rates. Formality and verbosity above 0.05 sig line, register marginal, tone flat.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Register marginal significance 对论文有两种 spinning：\n      (1) 如果 p<0.05，第三 working axis，C3 大幅强化；\n      (2) 如果 p=0.068，\"suggestive evidence consistent with C3, power-limited at n=100\"，\n      仍支持 \"axis-dependent sensitivity\" narrative。Either way，论文不受损。\n      NLI-only gate 的成功（0.91 vs joint 0.20）本身支持 \"BERTScore \n      is an unnecessarily strict bottleneck for vocabulary-changing axes\" 这一方法论发现。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"51205774-b602-4f29-ade2-87053aa668fb","total_cost_usd":0.41897375,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16949,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":11802,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16949,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11802,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16949},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":11907,"outputTokens":31,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.012062,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11802,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":16949,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.40691174999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"c16cb81e-cae4-41ef-8415-3b21dba4ab2f"}
